·             *YOU* extract it. This is for SECURITY REASONS!             ·

@{" Return to Introduction " Link INTRO!!}   @{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node FSIZES! "(2) Check for these file-sizes to make sure you have a GOOD Copy!"

    @{" Send.XIM   " Link SENDXIM}            17796 Bytes  --  Packs FilePackets
    @{" NetOnline  " Link ONLINE!}            15748 Bytes  --  UnPacks FilePackets
     NETSEND.info            1064 Bytes  --  SAMPLE BBSCMD Icon for Send
  NetOnline.guide           15593 Bytes  --  This Documentation

                        REQUIRED FILES & DIRECTORIES
                        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
<bbs location>AMIXNET/MYNODE.INFO           <-- Your NODE.ID
<bbs location>AMIXNET/UTILS/AXN             <-- Filepacket Generator
<bbs location>AMIXNET/OUTBOUND/             <-- Filepackets placed here
<bbs location>NODE<node>/WORK/              <-- Files unpacked here
<bbs location>AMIXNET/CONFS/<conf>/UPLOAD   <-- Files put online here
<bbs location>AMIXNET/FILEBASE              <-- Where Filepackets are
C:COPY                                      <-- Copy Files

<bbs location> can be "BBS:" , "WORK:BBS/" , "SYS:AMIEXPRESS/" .....
<node>         can be 0, 5, 32, 19, ....
<conf>         can be AX0001, PN0001, LS0003, CNS001, .....

@{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node SENDXIM "(3) The SEND.XIM Program Overview"

   SEND.XIM: This is a XIM door for AmiExpress. Read @{" INSTALLATION " Link INSTALL}
for the installation of SEND.XIM.  This program's function is to ask users
which files they want to upload&send. The user uploads a file (with ZModem)
to "<bbslocation>NODE<node>/WORK/", so make sure you have that directory.
After they finish uploading, they will be prompted to enter a 3-line file
description. The reason that it's only 3 lines is bcoz I don't think 
anybody will want to send really big files thru /XNet, considering the 
phone bills (erm!). Plus, I didn't see a reason to make it a full 8lines so
users can send asciis along with the files. 
   The description that the users enter will be called <filename>.AXN.
Please do not try to rename the files or delete the <filename>.AXN file, as
it will result in NO file-description on the receiving node.

@{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node ONLINE! "(4) The ONLINE.NET Program Overview"

   NetOnline  requires no config file, since it's all in the parameters.
Here are a few sample calls for NetOnline , from the CLI..

SAMPLE....NetOnline  AX0001 BBS: 1
SAMPLE....NetOnline  LS0001 SYS:AMIX/ 2
SAMPLE....NetOnline  CNS001 DH0:AMIEXPRESS/ 12

Breaking it down, here is what NetOnline  requires as parameters:

NetOnline AX0001 BBS: 1
^-.-----^ ^-.--^ ^-.^ ^
  |         |      |  |
  |         |      |  `-> Node #
  |         |      |   
  |         |      `-> Your BBS location
  |         |
  |         `-> Conference to process 
  |             (AX0001, PN0001, PFT001)
  |
  `-> Name & Path to NetOnline (bbs:amixnet/utils, bbs:utils, c:, so on)

@{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node SAMPLED "(4) Sample Entries...."

Here are some sample entries in your DIRx, Callerslog, and Files.Log files.

example DIRx       = bbs:amixnet/confs/alt001/DIR1
example callerslog = bbs:node1/callerslog
example files.log  = bbs:amixnet/logs/files.log

