@node INSTALL "(5) Installation "

Installation for NetOnline  is just to add a few lines in @{" FETCH.S " Link FETCH}

Installation for SEND.XIM is simple... in your bbs:commands/CONF<x>CMD
drawer!  BE SURE THAT IT IS A NETCONF.

For instance, let's say CONF5 was a NetConf. You'd Place NETSEND.INFO in
( BBS:COMMANDS/CONF5CMD/NETSEND.INFO )

( NETSEND.INFO TOOLTYPES )

        LOCATION=DOORS:SEND.XIM     <-- Location of the door
        TYPE=XIM                    <-- XIM door
        ACCESS=030                  <-- Access needed to use door
        PRIORITY=0                  <-- Priority (0)
        MULTINODE=YES               <-- Multinode (YES)
        STACK=4096                  <-- Stack for door (I set it at 4096)

@{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node FETCH "(4a) Example FETCH.S Entry"

----------* START: SAMPLE OF FETCH.S *----------
echo >>bbs:amixnet/logs/amixnet.log "-->Commanding /X to Collect Mail on " NOLINE
date >>bbs:amixnet/logs/amixnet.log
bbs:amixnet/scripts/pack.s
rx bbs:amixnet/scripts/syscmd.ced 1
run >nil: bbs:amixnet/scripts/schedule.s
bbs:amixnet/scripts/unpack.s
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline AX0001 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline PN0001 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline AX0002 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline LS0001 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline LS0003 BBS: 1
----------* END : SAMPLE OF FETCH.S *----------

The above entry would process all Filepackets for AX0001, PN0001, AX0002,
LS0001, and LS0003. Any other filepackets would be ignored.
You could also add an entire @{" script " Link SCRIPT} to FETCH.S .... it might be 
confusing but it works on my system!!

@{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node SCRIPT "Sample Script"

On my system I have an entire script for NetOnline  ... I think it's a bit
easier than editing 5 or so lines in fetch.s ..... here it is:

----------* START: FILES.S *----------
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline AX0001 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline PN0001 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline AX0002 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline LS0001 BBS: 1
bbs:amixnet/utils/NetOnline LS0003 BBS: 1
----------* END : FILES.S *----------

The call for the script is right after "unpack.s" ...
----------* START: SAMPLE OF FETCH.S *----------
echo >>bbs:amixnet/logs/amixnet.log "-->Commanding /X to Collect Mail on " NOLINE
date >>bbs:amixnet/logs/amixnet.log
bbs:amixnet/scripts/pack.s
rx bbs:amixnet/scripts/syscmd.ced 1
run >nil: bbs:amixnet/scripts/schedule.s
bbs:amixnet/scripts/unpack.s
bbs:amixnet/scripts/files.s
----------* END : SAMPLE OF FETCH.S *----------

You can think up of more ways to add this utility to your Fetch.s, but 
since I'm running out of space (I don't want this doc to be TOO long!!) 
I'll leave it alone...

@{" Return to FETCH.S " Link FETCH}   @{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
