@{" Possible Problems " Link PROBLEMS}

@{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
@node PROBLEMS " Possible Problems You Might Have..." 

» Filepackets are not being generated. (SEND.XIM)
  - Do you have the AXN utility? Get it from The OutLaw@305003!
  - Did you put AXN in <bbslocation>AMIXNET/UTILS/AXN ?
  - Are there any files in the <bbs location>:node<node>/WORK/ directory?
  - Is there a AMIXNET/OUTBOUND/ directory?

» I'm getting wierd filepackets generated. (SEND.XIM)
  - Did you put NETSEND.INFO in the CONF<x>CMD drawer or in the BBSCMD 
     drawer? Try putting NETSEND.INFO in a NetConf CMD drawer!
  - Does the Conference ID Exist?
  - Does the NodeID Exist?

» Filepackets are staying in the FILEBASE Directory (NetOnline)
  - In the call for NetOnline, did you specify THAT conference?
    Ex. NetOnline ALT001 BBS: 1  Would unpack YOUR filepackets for the 
     ALT001 conference ONLY. All other filepackets are left alone!
  - Is it your filepacket? ( F@<your node id>-<confid> )

» The files from a packet are not in my conference, but the entries are!
    (NetOnline)
  - Do you have a UPLOAD directory in that conference? NetOnline copies
    the non-.AXN files to <bbs location>/AMIXNET/CONFS/<conference>/UPLOAD.

» There is no DIRx entry in my NetConference, but the files are in the 
   UPLOAD directory! (NetOnline)
  - Do you have a DIR1 file in your NetConf?  If not, make one.

» I just got a Filepacket, and NetOnline extracted it, deleted it, and
   didn't put the files in the packet online! (NetOnline)
  - It's because the files did not have any descriptions....Since I'm not
    the best programmer I can't anticipate everything. I'm hoping that my
    program will become a "standard" /XNet utility. All we need is The
    OutLaw@305003 to use it, and I'm sure everybody will follow him (heh
    heh heh!)...

@{" Return to Bug Report Menu " Link UPDATES}   @{" Return to Main Menu " Link MAIN}
@endnode
